                                   pool's own arithmetic found, which is why
                                   the wording stays where bpa_reverse() and
                                   the pool are. lab/forward.sh produces them
                                   on a box, and test/test_prismash_refusals.py
                                   reads their widths. Where a forward is
                                   refused, and why each refusal exists. `sf`
                                   is completed rather than only checked:
                                   ip_pub and port_off are derived from the
                                   pool arithmetic, and deriving them here
                                   means the one place that decides a forward
                                   is legal is also the one place that says
